      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to State Government"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The executive structure of state government includes the Governor, Chief Minister, and Council of Ministers.",
        "State Legislature comprises two potential houses: Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) and Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad).",
        "Constitutional Articles define the executive, legislative, and administrative powers within Indian states.",
        "SSC exam preparation requires a strong grasp of constitutional provisions relating to state officials and legislative bodies."
      ],
