    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dagtu3n",
      "content": "• The State Legislature consists of the Governor and one or two houses."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b0zf1js",
      "content": "• States may have unicameral or bicameral legislature."
    },
    {
      "id": "lpz3ccm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r3sfk09",
      "content": "• Lower house of state legislature."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8ed3ulz",
      "content": "• Members directly elected by people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8gurdbk",
      "content": "• Normal term is 5 years."
    },
    {
      "id": "fl51x0k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ya442d7",
      "content": "• Upper house in some states."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional articles related to the Governor's executive powers and the Chief Minister's appointment are frequently asked in SSC exams.",
        "Differentiate between bicameral and unicameral state legislatures, focusing on Vidhan Sabha and Vidhan Parishad structures.",
        "Understand the constitutional role and collective responsibility of the state Council of Ministers."
      ],
      "id": "4k4hmo3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "47i2r7f",
      "content": "• It is a permanent body."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lv5upjl",
      "content": "• One-third members retire every two years."
    },
    {
      "id": "6rpxe8k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SSC / SSC Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t6ezwgz",
      "content": "• Part VI deals with State Government."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wef6t81",
      "content": "• Governor is constitutional head."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j4an1d0",
      "content": "• Chief Minister is real executive head."
    }
  ],
